-- title:
--   Connecting idele of an Eichler order of level N has index N²
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda_1$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order, in the sense that it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is maximal for inclusion among submodules with those four properties. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{A}}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, where $\widehat{\mathbb{A}}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. Write $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$, the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{A}}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the tensors $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components lie in the valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v$ at every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume: the image of $m$ lies in $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$; the scalar multiple $N\cdot m^{-1}$ lies in $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$; and the relative index of $\Lambda_1\cap\operatorname{conjByFiniteIdele}(\Lambda_1,m)$ in $\Lambda_1$, as additive groups, equals $N$, where $\operatorname{conjByFiniteIdele}(\Lambda_1,m)$ consists of those $q\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image $q\otimes 1$ lies in $m\,\widehat{\Lambda_1}\,m^{-1}$. Then for every unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{A}}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the relative index of the additive group of $\operatorname{ofFiniteIdele}(\Lambda_1,xm)=\{q: q\otimes 1\in xm\,\widehat{\Lambda_1}\}$ in that of $\operatorname{ofFiniteIdele}(\Lambda_1,x)=\{q: q\otimes 1\in x\,\widehat{\Lambda_1}\}$ equals $N^2$.
--
--   The hypotheses on $m$ say that $\Lambda_1\cap\operatorname{conjByFiniteIdele}(\Lambda_1,m)$ is an Eichler order of level $N$ with $\Lambda_1$ as one of its two end vertices, and the conclusion is the classical computation that a normalised connecting idele of such an order cuts a sublattice of index $N^2$ in every lattice class. It is the quaternionic input to the level-$N$ Deuring–Eichler dictionary, used in the construction of the bijection between the class set and the supersingular places in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace_ker`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace_ker).
